## Practical Metrics Calculations (With Examples)

### Metric 1: Sprint Velocity Forecasting

**Real Example - E-Commerce Platform Release Date:**

```
CURRENT STATE:
Backlog to complete: 200 points (all features for Q2 release)
Historical velocity:
├─ Sprint 1: 18 points
├─ Sprint 2: 21 points
├─ Sprint 3: 19 points
├─ Sprint 4: 22 points
├─ Sprint 5: 20 points
├─ Sprint 6: 21 points

CALCULATION:
Average velocity = (18+21+19+22+20+21) / 6 = 121 / 6 = 20.17 ≈ 20 points/sprint

FORECASTING:
Points remaining: 200
Velocity: 20 points/sprint
Number of sprints needed: 200 ÷ 20 = 10 sprints
Duration: 10 sprints × 2 weeks = 20 weeks = ~5 months

If starting Jan 15:
├─ Finish: ~June 15
├─ Buffer (10%): Add 1 week
└─ Release date: June 22 (realistic estimate)

STAKEHOLDER QUESTION: "Can we ship by May 1?"
Time available: ~15 weeks = 7.5 sprints
Capacity: 7.5 × 20 = 150 points
Scope must reduce: 200 - 150 = 50 points (must cut 25%)

OPTIONS PRESENTED:
1. Cut features (25% reduction needed)
2. Add team (risky, may reduce velocity)
3. Extend timeline to June 15 (recommended)
4. MVP approach: Release 150 points in May, rest June
```

